{"name":"Dead Lake","hex":"#2e5a88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dead","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["No longer living; deceased.","Devoid of living things; barren."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Exactly.","Very, absolutely, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chipola River","blocks":[{"text":"The Chipola River of northwestern Florida is a major tributary of the Apalachicola River. The upper part of the river flows over a karst terrain where it receives inflow from more than 60 springs. The lower part of the river flows over alluvial deposits of the Apalachicola Delta. Dead Lake, a natural impoundment, is part of the river."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Chipolarivermap.png/330px-Chipolarivermap.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chipola_River"},{"title":"Dead Lakes Park","blocks":[{"text":"Dead Lakes Park is a Gulf County park located 1 mile (1.6 km) north of Wewahitchka off Florida State Road 71."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Campground_entrance_at_Dead_Lakes_Park.jpg/330px-Campground_entrance_at_Dead_Lakes_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_Lakes_Park"},{"title":"Dead Lake (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Dead Lake is a 2019 Russian TV series. It is a production of TV3 Russia, and Mediaslovo. The show won a prize during Accolade Global Film Competition in United States, and also won local prizes in Russia, during a film festival in Omsk."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Dead_Lake_TV_series.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_Lake_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Death","blocks":[{"text":"Death is the end of an organism's life. It is the irreversible cessation of biological functions that sustain a living organism. Entropy, nature's tendency toward disorder, can contribute to the breakdown of living systems over time. Upon death, organisms stop exhibiting behavior and generally begin to decompose through various physical and chemical processes. Death can occur at any stage of development, including in infancy. A person may experience clinical death that is reversible, resulting in some cases in a near-death experience. In humans, establishing death of the brain determines that an individual has irreversibly died."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Hendrick_Andriessen_-_Vanity_Piece_-_1914-DE_-_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_Ghent_%28MSK%29.jpg/330px-Hendrick_Andriessen_-_Vanity_Piece_-_1914-DE_-_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_Ghent_%28MSK%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg/500px-Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg/1280px-Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg/500px-Willis_Bridge_over_Chipola_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Wilis Bridge in Calhoun County","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/